All 15 tests pass, 0 failures, no TypeScript runtime errors. The fixed cases from the spec (`€1.234,56`, `$1,234`, `€1 234`, `-€5`, `($1,234)`, `€1.23`, etc.) all behave as required.

I added one extra case beyond your list (`'10 GBP' → { cents: 1000, currency: 'GBP' }`) because the spec's five "$"-style tokens already imply code-after-amount works, and it fit naturally alongside the listed `£10` test — the currency tests already cover token-before and token-after for EUR/USD, so GBP code-after is a consistent completion. No other deviations from the plan.
